You woke up lying on the pavement. The full moon had already shown up from behind the roof and was shining brightly in your face. Not a single soul was around.
"Weird, how long have I been lying here? Nobody even called an ambulance," you thought to yourself, slowly walking along the street. In the distance you heard the sound of sirens. You turned round the corner and faced a group of people.
"Wolf! Wolf!" someone screamed. People rushed in all directions. Saving yourself from the beast, you ran together with them. You looked back a couple of times, full of fright, expecting to see an open toothy mouth, but there was nothing behind you. Finally you decided to separate yourself from the mad group and turned into an alleyway and hid behind a garbage can. You carefully looked from behind the cover and saw two policemen. They were walking right towards you.
"The wolf really is here, then!" you thought to yourself, growing cold with fear.  You nervously began to look around. Suddenly you saw something dark and hairy by the opposite wall. Your heart thumped loudly and your ears were ringing in fear. The next moment, in spite of the panic clutching at your chest, you made a frightening discovery: on the opposite wall you were looking into a mirror that someone had thrown away. The reflection in it was yours!
"I'm a monster!" you screamed with despair. But the police officers heard only a terrifying howling. It became clear that they were coming to kill you. You needed to run! But where? To the left and right there were houses. Behind them was a three meter concrete fence and a bunch of armed men in front of it.